1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,504
Welcome to Absolute ADAS.

2
00:00:02,854 --> 00:00:10,806
This training walks you through filing and paying our quarterly excise tax return with the Washington State Department of Revenue, also called DOR.

3
00:00:11,155 --> 00:00:18,564
You'll see the real screens from Zoho Books and My DOR. Keep the runbook open while you watch. It has every step as a checklist.

4
00:00:20,163 --> 00:00:22,579
Washington doesn't have a state income tax.

5
00:00:22,929 --> 00:00:28,833
Instead, businesses pay B&O tax, which stands for business and occupation, on gross receipts.

6
00:00:29,183 --> 00:00:33,071
We report ours under one line, Service and Other Activities.

7
00:00:33,421 --> 00:00:37,997
The return is filed and paid online in My DOR, once every quarter.

8
00:00:39,597 --> 00:00:43,053
Quarterly returns are due on the last day of the month after the quarter ends.

9
00:00:43,403 --> 00:00:48,923
That's April thirtieth, July thirty-first, October thirty-first, and January thirty-first.

10
00:00:49,273 --> 00:00:57,081
If the due date lands on a weekend or holiday, it moves to the next business day. My DOR shows the exact due date at the top of the return.

11
00:00:57,431 --> 00:01:03,927
For example, the fourth quarter 2026 return is due Monday, February first, 2027.

12
00:01:04,277 --> 00:01:08,757
Our target is to have it filed by the twentieth of the due month, well before the deadline.

13
00:01:10,357 --> 00:01:13,045
Part one. Get the number from Zoho Books.

14
00:01:13,395 --> 00:01:16,243
In Zoho Books, click Reports in the left menu.

15
00:01:16,593 --> 00:01:19,745
Under Report Category, click Payments Received.

16
00:01:21,345 --> 00:01:26,321
In the Payments Received category, open the report also called Payments Received.

17
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:30,817
Set the date range to Previous Quarter and run the report.

18
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:36,847
Check the dates under the company name. For the third quarter, it should say July first through September thirtieth.

19
00:01:37,197 --> 00:01:42,989
Then click Export and choose PDF. Save the PDF. It's our backup for the return.

20
00:01:43,339 --> 00:01:48,011
Scroll to the bottom of the report. The TOTAL line is the number you'll enter in My DOR.

21
00:01:49,611 --> 00:01:51,723
Part two. File in My DOR.

22
00:01:52,073 --> 00:02:01,225
Go to secure.dor.wa.gov and sign in with your own SecureAccess Washington login. Mark adds you as a user. Never share a login.

23
00:02:01,575 --> 00:02:07,607
Select Absolute ADAS LLC, find the open return for the quarter, and click File return.

24
00:02:07,957 --> 00:02:11,845
Double-check the period. Filing the wrong quarter is the most common mistake.

25
00:02:13,445 --> 00:02:16,485
The first screen lists our tax classifications.

26
00:02:16,835 --> 00:02:20,643
Keep the same classifications as last period, and click Next.

27
00:02:20,993 --> 00:02:25,185
Never click Add or Delete Tax Classifications without asking Mark first.

28
00:02:26,785 --> 00:02:34,017
On the Business and Occupation screen, type the Zoho TOTAL into Gross Amount on the Service and Other Activities line.

29
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:39,935
In this example, that's $74,725.61.

30
00:02:40,285 --> 00:02:42,029
Leave Retailing at zero.

31
00:02:42,379 --> 00:02:48,603
My DOR calculates the tax automatically at 1.5%. You don't add deductions or credits.

32
00:02:48,953 --> 00:02:50,025
Then click Next.

33
00:02:51,625 --> 00:02:57,465
On State Sales and Use, Retail Sales stays at zero. We don't collect retail sales tax.

34
00:02:57,815 --> 00:03:02,343
If you ever see sales tax on one of our invoices, stop and ask Mark.

35
00:03:02,693 --> 00:03:03,637
Click Next.

36
00:03:05,237 --> 00:03:11,909
On Local Sales, the Lake Stevens line, location code 3109, also stays at zero.

37
00:03:12,259 --> 00:03:14,723
The Difference box at the bottom should read zero.

38
00:03:15,073 --> 00:03:15,825
Click Next.

39
00:03:17,425 --> 00:03:22,161
The Summary screen shows the line you filed. Check that the period and gross amount are right.

40
00:03:22,511 --> 00:03:25,647
Fill in Prepared By with your name, and your phone number.

41
00:03:25,997 --> 00:03:30,205
For email, use ar@absoluteadas.com.

42
00:03:30,555 --> 00:03:35,371
For the Buyers Sales and Use Preference Addendum question, choose No. Then click Next.

43
00:03:36,971 --> 00:03:39,147
Return Totals shows what we owe.

44
00:03:39,497 --> 00:03:46,585
Estimated Penalty and Estimated Interest should be zero. They only show up when a return is late, like in this example.

45
00:03:46,935 --> 00:03:50,359
Don't check Request Penalty Waiver on your own. Ask Mark.

46
00:03:50,709 --> 00:03:51,573
Click Next.

47
00:03:53,173 --> 00:03:59,349
For Payment Method, choose Bank Account, ACH Debit. It's free, and it's how we always pay.

48
00:03:59,699 --> 00:04:05,459
Don't use a card. The processor charges a 2.96% fee. And never choose No Payment.

49
00:04:05,809 --> 00:04:10,881
On the next screen, confirm our bank account and set the payment date on or before the due date.

50
00:04:12,481 --> 00:04:19,697
On Review and Submit, check four things: total amount due, payment method, payment effective date, and payment amount.

51
00:04:20,047 --> 00:04:25,103
The payment amount must match the total amount due, and the date must be on or before the due date.

52
00:04:25,453 --> 00:04:32,189
Click Submit once. Submitting authorizes DOR to debit our bank account, so never pay the same return a second way.

53
00:04:33,789 --> 00:04:35,965
Last step. Save your proof.

54
00:04:36,315 --> 00:04:40,379
Write down the confirmation number and download a PDF of the filed return.

55
00:04:40,729 --> 00:04:44,713
Save it alongside the Zoho Payments Received PDF for that quarter.

56
00:04:45,063 --> 00:04:50,983
A day or two after the payment date, check the bank account to confirm the debit went through, and let Mark know it's done.

57
00:04:52,583 --> 00:04:54,503
Here's why the deadline matters.

58
00:04:54,853 --> 00:04:59,397
If the tax isn't paid by the due date, DOR adds a nine percent penalty.

59
00:04:59,747 --> 00:05:06,451
It jumps to nineteen percent after the end of the following month, and twenty-nine percent after the end of the second month, plus interest.

60
00:05:06,801 --> 00:05:09,873
Even in a quarter with no receipts, we still have to file.

61
00:05:10,223 --> 00:05:14,767
If there's ever a problem paying, file on time anyway and tell Mark right away.

62
00:05:16,367 --> 00:05:19,391
Some other quarterly filings are not part of this return.

63
00:05:19,741 --> 00:05:27,213
Employment Security, or ESD, handles unemployment insurance, Paid Family and Medical Leave, and WA Cares.

64
00:05:27,563 --> 00:05:33,787
Labor and Industries handles the workers' comp quarterly report, and federal estimated taxes go to the IRS.

65
00:05:34,137 --> 00:05:38,153
Each one has its own system and deadlines. Those are covered separately.

66
00:05:39,753 --> 00:05:45,033
To recap: in Zoho, run Payments Received for the previous quarter and grab the total.

67
00:05:45,383 --> 00:05:51,383
In My DOR, put that total on the Service and Other Activities line, and leave everything else at zero.

68
00:05:51,733 --> 00:05:57,413
Fill in the summary, pay by ACH debit, check the review screen, submit, and save your proof.

69
00:05:57,763 --> 00:06:05,971
If anything doesn't look right, ask Mark first. DOR's information line is 360-705-6705.

70
00:06:06,321 --> 00:06:08,657
Thanks for watching, and welcome to the team.
